  "title": "Azure VPN Gateway \u2014 Complete Observability",
  "description": "End-to-end Datadog dashboard for Azure VPN Gateway: tunnel state and IPsec SAs, throughput, packet drops, BGP and routing, Point-to-Site, gateway capacity vs SKU limits, NAT rules, connection resources, Virtual WAN gateways and diagnostic logs. Built on the Datadog Azure integration.",
  "widgets": [
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "\ud83d\udcd6 Read me first \u2014 metric mapping, tags, SKU limits",
        "background_color": "gray",
        "show_title": true,
        "type": "group",
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "type": "note",
              "content": "## Azure VPN Gateway \u2014 full observability dashboard\n\n**Data source:** Datadog Azure integration (Azure Monitor metrics pulled per resource).\n\n| Azure resource type | Datadog metric namespace | Covered in |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworkGateways` | `azure.network_virtualnetworkgateways.*` | most groups |\n| `Microsoft.Network/connections` | `azure.network_connections.*` | *Connection resources* |\n| `Microsoft.Network/vpnGateways` (Virtual WAN) | `azure.network_vpngateways.*` | *Virtual WAN* |\n\n**Tags used** \u2014 Datadog default Azure tags: `subscription_name`, `subscription_id`, `resource_group`,\n`region`, `name` (the gateway resource name), `type`, `cloud_provider`.\nAzure Monitor **dimensions** arrive as lowercase tags: `connectionname`, `remoteip`, `instance`,\n`bgppeeraddress`, `protocol`, `natrule`, `droptype`, `flowtype`, `routetype`.\n\n**Before you rely on it:**\n1. In *Metrics \u2192 Summary* search `azure.network_virtualnetworkgateways` and confirm the metric names below\n   exist in your org. Datadog only emits a metric once Azure has published at least one datapoint for it,\n   so unused features (NAT rules, P2S, BGP) will show \"No data\" until they are in use \u2014 that is expected.\n2. Check the dimension tags on one metric (Metrics Explorer \u2192 the metric \u2192 *Tags*). If your org shows\n   e.g. `connection_name` instead of `connectionname`, do a find/replace on this JSON before importing.\n3. Metric polling granularity for VPN Gateway is 5 minutes (P2S metrics 1 minute), so avoid sub-5m windows.\n\n**Tunnel \"up\" signal:** Azure has no boolean tunnel-state metric. `QmsaCount` (IPsec Quick-Mode SAs)\nis the practical proxy \u2014 `qmsa_count = 0` on a configured tunnel means the tunnel is down.\n`MmsaCount` (Main-Mode SA) tells you whether IKE phase 1 is established.\n\n**VPN Gateway SKU limits** (for the capacity group):\n\n| SKU | Aggregate throughput | S2S/VNet2VNet tunnels | P2S connections |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Basic | 100 Mbps | 10 | 128 (SSTP only) |\n| VpnGw1 / VpnGw1AZ | 650 Mbps | 30 | 128 SSTP + 250 IKEv2/OpenVPN |\n| VpnGw2 / VpnGw2AZ | 1 Gbps (Gen2: 1.25 Gbps) | 30 | 128 SSTP + 500 |\n| VpnGw3 / VpnGw3AZ | 1.25 Gbps (Gen2: 2.5 Gbps) | 30 | 128 SSTP + 1,000 |\n| VpnGw4 / VpnGw4AZ | 5 Gbps | 100 | 128 SSTP + 5,000 |\n| VpnGw5 / VpnGw5AZ | 10 Gbps | 100 | 128 SSTP + 10,000 |\n\n**Logs group** requires Azure diagnostic settings for the gateway\n(`GatewayDiagnosticLog`, `TunnelDiagnosticLog`, `RouteDiagnosticLog`, `IKEDiagnosticLog`, `P2SDiagnosticLog`)\nforwarded to Datadog via Event Hub. Adjust the `source:`/`@category` facets to match your pipeline.",
              "background_color": "blue",
              "font_size": "14",
              "text_align": "left",
              "vertical_align": "top",
              "show_tick": false,
              "tick_pos": "50%",
              "tick_edge": "left",
              "has_padding": true
            },
            "layout": {
